Locked phrasing (SOV-Counter-Canon #2): Article 50 transparency obligations apply from 2 August 2026.

That date has already passed. Enforcement is live. Do not treat this as a future cliff.

What Article 50 is (and is not):

- Art. 50(1): tell people they are interacting with an AI system at first interaction, unless obvious. Accessibility applies.
- Art. 50(2): machine-readable marking of synthetic audio/image/video/text. Grace until 2 December 2026 only for generative systems already on the market before 2 August 2026. Anything launched after 2 Aug 2026 has no grace.
- Art. 50(3): inform people exposed to emotion recognition or biometric categorisation.
- Art. 50(4): label deepfakes; disclose AI-generated public-interest text unless a person holds editorial responsibility after human review.

Article 50 is not Article 5 (prohibited practices — in force 2 Feb 2025). It is not the GSPC axis "art5-safeguard". Do not mix those three.

Fines for transparency breaches: up to EUR 15 million or 3% worldwide turnover (higher tiers exist for other articles).

Our surfaces: public registry at https://councilof.ai/ai-transparency
Article 50 page: https://councilof.ai/article-50
Provenance finding (marks in the wild): 0 of 20 assets survived — measurement, not a marking certificate.

Do not announce: Article 50 compliant, transparency certified, passed Council.

GPAI provider duties began 2 Aug 2025; legacy GPAI placed on the market before that date has until 2 Aug 2027. That is a different clock from Art. 50.

Measurement, never certification.
